1
00:05:52,941 --> 00:05:58,941
Just 10 seconds . . . to save a dream from becoming a nuclear nightmare.

2
00:11:45,882 --> 00:11:51,882
Earth II is a tv movie, science fiction film directed by Tom Gries.

3
00:17:38,823 --> 00:17:44,823
In the near future, a space station dubbed Earth II is built for
the purpose of scientific research and world peace.

4
00:23:31,764 --> 00:23:37,764
However, that peace is shattered when the Chinese send up a nuclear bomb
that is orbiting just a few miles away from the station.

5
00:29:24,705 --> 00:29:30,705
Can the crew disarm the bomb before it detonates, not only
destroying the station but setting off World War III?

6
00:35:17,647 --> 00:35:23,647
David Seville, played by Gary Lockwood.

7
00:41:10,588 --> 00:41:16,588
Jim Capa, played by Scott Hylands.

8
00:47:03,529 --> 00:47:09,529
Dr. Loren Huxley, played by Hari Rhodes.

9
00:52:56,470 --> 00:53:02,470
Frank Karger, played by Anthony Franciosa.

10
00:58:49,411 --> 00:58:55,411
Lisa Karger, played by Mariette Hartley.

11
01:04:42,352 --> 01:04:48,352
Walter Dietrich, played by Gary Merrill.

12
01:10:35,294 --> 01:10:41,294
Earth II is a 1971 pilot, aired November 28 (and released theatrically outside North America),
for a television series about a colony established in orbit around the Earth.

13
01:16:28,235 --> 01:16:34,235
A WABE Production in association with Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer Television, it
starred Gary Lockwood, Scott Hylands and Hari Rhodes.

14
01:22:21,176 --> 01:22:27,176
The film was written and produced by William Read Woodfield
and Allan Balter, and directed by Tom Gries.

15
01:28:14,117 --> 01:28:20,117
The film explores themes of space colony, space station,
nuclear threat, spacewalk, space walk.

16
01:34:07,058 --> 01:34:13,058
The tone is thought_provoking.
